window.products.push({"id":93808,"name":"807047901 Dishwasher Water Inlet Valve (OEM) by Blutoget - Compatible with Frigi-daire Ken-more Dishwasher - Replaces 33199020 3315025 AP5948913 PS986","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":0.0,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61xbauLQoJL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","description":"Durable Stainless Steel and ABS ✅ 【PRODUCT SPECIFICATIONS 】: 807047901 water inlet valve supplies water to the dishwasher. 120V/60HZ. This is a new GENUIN replacement part.33199020 valve keep your dishwasher running smoothly at all times.Made of high quality and durable stainless steel and abs material, not easy to rust, not easy to break, maximize the service life.Help you solve various problems. ✅ 【GREAT VALUE PACK】 : Includes 1 x 807047901 water inlet valve.Product Dimensions: ‎4 x 2.7 x 2.4 inches. It can solve these problems that the dishwasher leaks, does not drain or does not circulate water.If the dishwasher does not wash properly, replacing the 807047901 water inlet valve in time can effectively keep the dishwasher running for a long time. Make sure the replacement is compatible with your appliance before purchasing. ✅ 【365 DAYS GUARANTEE】: Blutoget Dishwasher Water Inlet Valve supports 365 DAYS return and exchange. We promise to ensure your absolute satisfaction with every purchase. Risk-free shopping, If you have any quality problem during warranty period, please contact customer service in time. We will try our best to solve the problem. Customer satisfaction is our tireless pursuit. ✅【REPLACEMENT PART No.】:807047901(OEM) Dishwasher Water Inlet Valve compatible Frigi-daire.Replaces PD00025455, 807047901, 3315025, AP594891, PS9865067, EAP9865067, 33199020 etc. If you are not sure whether it is suitable for your machine, please contact us in time, we will be happy to help you solve this problem. ✅【EASY TO INSTALL】:Please disconnect the power and water supply of the dishwasher, wear work gloves to ensure hand safety before install 807047901, you will need tools wrench, screwdrivers, plyers.To pull the dishwasher out to get enough room.Took the washer bottom cover off, removed hoses, electrical contacts, and screws for the housing to take out the inlet valve, reconnected the water line and wire harness. Slid the washer back into place. Turned on the water valve. Watched for leaks.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61xbauLQoJL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"Blutoget","source_asin":"B08RYGR42M","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-93808","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B08RYGR42M","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B08RYGR42M","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
